{"url": "https://www.dbs.nus.edu.sg/education/graduates/doctor-of-philosophy/", "final_url": "https://www.dbs.nus.edu.sg/education/graduates/doctor-of-philosophy/", "status": 200, "method": "chromium", "fetched": "2026-11-14", "text": "Privacy Notice\nThis site uses cookies. By clicking accept or continuing to use this site, you agree to our use of cookies. For more details, please see our Privacy Policy.\nAccept\nNUS News\nStudent\nStaff\nContact Us\nHome\nAbout Us\nOverview\nHead\u2019s Welcome\nManagement Team\nBrief History\nPeople\nFaculty\nAll Faculty\nBioPhysical Sciences\nCell, Molecular and Developmental Biology\nEcology, Evolution and Biodiversity\nAdjunct Faculty\nAdministration\nLaboratory Support\nEmeritus Professors and Honorary Fellows\nEducation\nUndergraduate\nGraduates\nResearch Programmes\nDoctor of Philosophy\nCoursework Programmes\nMSc Biotechnology\nMSc Biodiversity Conservation and Sustainability\nMSc Forensic Science\nStudent Highlights\nResearch\nResearch Focus\nBiophysical Sciences (BPS)\nCell, Molecular & Developmental Biology (CMDB)\nEcology & Evolutionary Biology (EEB)\nCentres, Museum and Facilities\nCentre for BioImaging Sciences (CBIS)\nProtein and Proteomics Centre (PPC)\nResearch Centre on Sustainable Urban Farming (SUrF)\nSelected Research Publications\nResearch News at the Faculty of Science\nCareers\nJobs in DBS\nNUS Presidential Young Professorship (PYP)\nJobs for Life Sciences Alumni\nOutreach\nOutreach Talks\nWorkshops and Learning Journeys\nAmgen Scholars Program\nSummer Course \u2013 Chemistry of Life\nAlumni\nLatest Events\nNews & Events\nNews\nEvents\nSeminars\nDoctor of Philosophy\nHome\nEducation\nGraduate Studies\nDoctor of Philosophy\nDEPARTMENT OF BIOLOGICAL SCIENCES\nDOCTOR OF PHILOSOPHY\nInformation for Prospective Students\nInformation for Current Students\nAdmission and Application Information\nHello and welcome!\nAre you considering embarking on a PhD in Biological Sciences journey?\nWe have a strong research culture centred around three main research foci: Cell, Molecular and Developmental Biology; Ecology, Biodiversity and Environmental Biology; and Biophysical Sciences, Computational and Structural Biology.\nWe boast world-class academics who are dedicated in their research work as they are in your graduate experience. You will get a chance to study under and work alongside them for your experience here in NUS. Here, you will partake in research using state-of-the-art facilities.\nOn top of that, we have a strong publication record. Every year, over half of the scientific papers from our department are contributed by graduate students alone. Many of the papers are published in the top scientific journals such as Nature, Science, Cell, Nature Genetics, Nature Immunology, Nature Biotechnology, Nature Structural Biology, Current Biology, Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences USA, EMBO Journal, etc.\nOur department is consistently amongst the top ranked by subjects \u2013 just this year, we were in the top 15 globally according to the QS World University Rankings by Subject 2025.\nApplication for admissions are open all year round so come be a part of our community today!\nAdmission Criteria\nApplication Information\nNUS Singapore/PR Graduate Fellowship SGF (formerly known as the Graduate Tutor Scheme)\nEarly Offer Admissions\nScholarships\nContact Us\nInformation for Current PhD Students\nCourses and Timetable\nCoursework Requirements\nLaboratory Rotation Programme\nThesis Advisory Committee (TAC)\nQualifying Examinations (QE)\nThesis Submission\nOral Examination\nGraduate Part-Time Teaching (PTT)\nDepartmental Seminars\nGraduate Congress\nFinancial Assistance for Attending International Conference\nAwards and Recognition\nForms\nOther Information\nContact Us\nDepartment of Biological Sciences\nNational University of Singapore Block S3 #05-01 16 Science Drive 4 Singapore 117558\n\u00a9 National University of Singapore. All rights Reserved.\nLegal", "links": [["Pri